From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] net: ethernet: mtk_wed: handle a failed init_rx_buf

mtk_wed_rx_buffer_alloc() ignores the return value of init_rx_buf.
mt76_wed_init_rx_buf() releases all rx tokens and returns -ENOMEM if an
allocation fails. mtk_wed_rx_buffer_hw_init() then gives the rx buffer
manager rx_npkt descriptors with no valid buffer.

Free the descriptors and return the error, so that mtk_wed_start()
returns before it starts the device, as for the other allocation
failures.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
@@ -854,7 +854,13 @@ mtk_wed_rx_buffer_alloc(struct mtk_wed_d
 
 	dev->rx_buf_ring.desc = desc;
 	dev->rx_buf_ring.desc_phys = desc_phys;
-	dev->wlan.init_rx_buf(dev, dev->wlan.rx_npkt);
+	if (dev->wlan.init_rx_buf(dev, dev->wlan.rx_npkt)) {
+		dma_free_coherent(dev->hw->dev,
+				  dev->wlan.rx_nbuf * sizeof(*desc),
+				  desc, desc_phys);
+		dev->rx_buf_ring.desc = NULL;
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	}
 
 	return mtk_wed_hwrro_buffer_alloc(dev);
 }
